From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:35:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] host: GetAddrInfo through the Nextendo map
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

nn::socket::GetAddrInfo no longer answers EAI_FAIL unconditionally: with DM_NEXTENDO=1 a name
in the map resolves to the mapped address, anything else goes to the real resolver, and with
the switch off the answer is the EAI_FAIL it always was.

The resolver builds Horizon's addrinfo itself (libnx's FreeBSD field order: canonname before
addr, 16-byte sockaddr_in, network byte order) instead of handing back the system's chain, and
FreeAddrInfo frees that chain. Plain C, no hle.h, so t_nextendo_gai runs off Darwin too — the
map, the wildcard, a hint's socktype, a real name, a name that cannot resolve, and the switch
off are all checked.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: with every online service cut, upstream answers EAI_FAIL for ever; the fork needs a resolver that can be pointed at Nextendo, and keeps it behind DM_NEXTENDO
Issue: none opened yet — notes/nextendo-spike.md carries the plan and the open question for Nextendo

